==English==

===Etymology===
Of German origin, meaning "to be fashionable"; made popular during the reign of King George III of England in the 1780s.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of [[dapper]] attire.

====Usage notes====
Restricted to the rural areas on the east coast of Scotland.

